   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A path that visits each vertex exactly once is a Hamilton path. Recall that a path is a walk that has no repeated vertices or edges. An Euler trail uses every edge exactly once.</p>\n<p>It does not need to start and end on the same vertex.</p>\n<p>This is a Hamilton path. It is not an Euler trail because it does not use every edge. It does not use <i>bc</i> or <i>ae</i>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Hamilton path"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
