     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A path that visits each vertex exactly once is a Hamilton path. Recall that a path is a walk that has no repeated vertices or edges. An Euler trail uses every edge exactly once.</p>\n<p>This is neither. It does not visit every edge nor does it visit every vertex.</p>"
